INFO 8599 :: Page 121 :: 1.35 P. m City Pt Feby 22nd 1865 12 M to Secy of War . I do not think Gen Crook & Gen Kelly should be mustered out of service before there is an investigation of the circumstances of their capture . It may prove they had taken proper precautions and the neglect has been the fault of someone else . I think Gen Humphreys will prove one of our best Corps Commanders , hence I would not care to have him leave here . I asked Gen Halleck some time since to order Gen Crocker from New Mexico . If he is within reach I scarcely know his equal to take Crooks place If he cannot be reached I will name someone else , probably Terry who from the number of Division Commanders with Schofields Army ranking him is occupying an unimportant position ---- US Grant 7.30 PM 7.45 P. M Point City Feby 22nd 1865 Brig Gen Wm Hoffman . Please send for Exchange all Naval prisoners at Fort Lafayette Ft Delaware . If Campbell & Mars have not been sent from Johnsons Island have them sent forward at once . Some fifteen thousand of our prisoners will be received with in the next six days taking all in Virginia & North Carolina & those that were in South Carolina . U. S. Grant Lt Genl
INFO 8600 :: Page 122 :: 745 P. M 730 P. M City Pt Feby 22nd 1865 Maj Gen H. W. Halleck Please order Gen Gillmore to send here all rebel prisoners in his Department for exchange ---- U. S. Grant Lt Genl 11 PM City Pt Feb 22.1865 10 PM Br Gen W. Hoffman C. G. P. please direct the discharge of Chas. a. Peabody rebel prisoner confined at Camp Douglas on his taking the oath of allegiance US Grant Lt Gen 1100 PM City Point Feb 22 1865 22d 11 PM Secy War all points on the coast now being taken from the rebels except Mobile if Wilmington is not now in our possession it will be within forty eight hours I think makes me believe that the French rebel rams will go to Mobile Bay to cut off our troops there from supplies ---- I have good reasons to believe orders have gone from Richmond to hold Mobile at all hazard ---- this strengthens this theory ---- these rams may have started for a different destination but as they will likely stop at some port near our coast to fill up with coal & supplies they can get final orders I think it advisable to notify the Navy Dept & Gen Canby of this theory so they can prepare for it sig US Grant
INFO 8601 :: Page 123 :: 12 PM W R Plum Nashville City Point Feb 22 1865 Twenty two 11 PM For Gen Thomas I heard it from good authority that orders have gone from Richmond to the comdr at Mobile to hold that city to the last ---- This will cause a concentration of the rebel forces in that quarter & make your cavalry expedition effective & easy & will tend in the end to secure all we want without a long march into the interior by our Infy force ---- US Grant Lt Gen 10.05 AM Ft Monroe Va Feby 23rd 1865 Hd Qrs Army of the Ohio Feby 19th via Ft Monroe 23rd for Gen Grant City Pt . Day before yesterday Cox' Division moved to Smithville & then toward Fort Anderson . Yes = = terday it closed up on Fort Anderson & entrenched a line under navy fire close to the enemy's to be held by two Brigades . with the balance of his command & Ame's Division , which had been sent to Smithville , Cox then was started on the flank movement for the rear of Fort Anderson making about ten miles by dark . The enemy evacuated Fort Anderson during the night and the lines in front of Terry this morning . They will at once be followed toward Wilmington (sig) C B Comstock Lt Col A. D. C &c (another) Hd Qrs Dept of N. C. Fort Anderson Feby 19th for Gen Grant City Pt . Genl I have the honor to report the success of our operations
INFO 7779 :: Page 121 :: 10 am Fort Monroe Feby 21st 65 H'd Qrs. Dept. of the South Hilton Head S. C. Feby 17th via Ft Monroe 21st for Gen Grant ---- & Genl Halleck . Genl. I send you by mail Charleston newspapers papers of the 8th 9th 10th & 11th which give the latest news from Sherman. They state that he crossed the South fork of the Edisto at Pinnakers Bridge on the ninth . I have possession of the Charleston & Savannah RR as far as the Edisto. The enemy are on the line of the Edisto at Jacksonboro and Willstown. Genl Hatche's Division captured six guns on the fifteenth the road has been so thoroughly Destroyed that there is no use of keeping up the entrenched camp at Pocotaligo Station. I can make much better use of the troops elsewhere & ask authority to use my discretion in the matter. The place can at any time be occupied in a few hours . I have no dispatches from Bulls bay later than the twelfth. General Potter expected to land there on the thirteenth. I shall go up there tomorrow I have the honor to be Genl Very Respy Obt Sent QA Gillmore M Genl
INFO 7780 :: Page 122 :: 8 PM Balto Feby 21st 1865 7 pm for Secy of War In Response to inquiries our agent at Cumberland advises namely "Genls Kelly and Crook were taken out of their beds about three oclock by a rebel force variously estimated from fifty to hundred and fifty but I think there was not more than fifty ---- They took the watch - man at Depot and two oprs and kept them for some time ---- As soon as the watch man got off he came and called me which was about four oclock ---- I got up and came down but they had all left ---- Upon inquiry I found they had gone down the tow path after taking Genl K & C and Adjt Melvin and fifteen or twenty horses ---- The Engineers of stock trains which were just arriving saw them ---- Our cavalry was sent in pursuit and over took them about Romney but nothing definite known ---- Genl Lightburn left here by a special engine about five thirty PM for new Creek to send out parties to various points to guard the outlets ---- only rebel officer heard of was a Lieut Mac Neil ---- Two stores were broken open but not much damage or goods taken ---- no interferance with with the of trains ---- there are rumors of three rebel Brigades under Rosser Lee . and Paine in vicinity of Moorfield it is unknown whose command was in Cumberland " up to this hour six twenty five pm we have been unable to ascertain any thing more definite J W. Garrett
INFO 7781 :: Page 123 :: Winchester Va Feb 21" 1865 Feb 21st To Gen Grant ---- I would prefer Gibbon to either Humphrey or Gen Warren if you can let me have him ---- If not I prefer Humphrey to Warren. there is and has been an unexcusable carelessness on the part of the officers & troops in the Dept of West Virginia I have discussed subject to the approval of the President in all cases ---- There is on the Balto & Ohio Railroad or covering it from Martinsburg to Parkersburg fourteen thousand effective troops and there was at Cumberland of this force between thirty five hundred and four thousand men, still they have been asking for more I hope to get off from here about Saturday if possible ---- I have a canvass pontoon train enroute from Washn which I would like to take ---- PH Sheridan Maj Genl 130 City Point Feby 22d 1865 To Maj Gen Halleck ---- Please direct Gen Humphreys who is now in Washn to return immediately to his command He has yet four or five days leave which he will have to take another time, when he can be better spared US Grant Lt Genl
INFO 7782 :: Page 124 :: 3.05 P. M City Point Va Feby 22nd 1865 22nd 130 PM Gen Sheridan ---- Paines Brigade of Cavalry has arrived here from the Valley. Wickhams brigade arrived some time since. Two passenger trains and two freight trains are now run daily over the centr = = al road there is also great activity on the Fredericksburg road many supplies have been collected in the northern neck and many more are smuggled in from Phila and other places and taken to Richmond over this road. 70,000 pounds of bacon alone have gone to Richmond the last week over that road. Cannot Augur send a force to break that trade up? It is reported that all troops from the Valley except those brought here have gone to Lynchburg ---- US Grant 11 AM Fort Monroe Feby 23d 1865 U S S. Rhode Island Hampton Roads 23d for Secy Navy. The newberne has arrived from Cape fear river which place she left on the twenty first inst ---- her Comdr reports that our forces were within four miles of Wilmington ---- heavy fighting was going on and our forces were still advancing ---- Very Resp fully Stephen Trenchard Comdr
INFO 7783 :: Page 125 :: 5 P. M Pickwith City Pt Winchester Va Feby 23rd 1865 To Gen Grant. I have teleghed Gen Augur in reference to the Northern neck there is also in Loudon & king & Queen Counties and in fact in the section of country from Bowling Green down to Urbanna between the Rappahannock & Mattapony rivers a large amount of provisions & forage ---- Last summer when I was in this section I found the finest crops of corn I ever saw & every acre was planted I think some supplies are being gathered west of the of the Shenandoah Valley in the Little Mountain Valley from Warm Springs to Paris burg on New river. Rossens Brigade of Cavy also Imbodens Jacksons & McCauslands are in the above named section. It has been raining here for the last twelve hours the snow is going fast ---- P. H. Sheridan Maj Genl
INFO 7805 :: Page 147 :: 130 pm to Beckwith Nashville Mch 6th 1865 10 am 6th for Lt Gen Grant. We have had a very heavy storm which has retarded the commencement of operations in this Dept by swelling the streams and destroying RR bridges but I am in hopes Wilson has started by this time ---- Stoneman will reach Knoxville by Saturday next with his expeditionary force and will start from there im'my . I will then adjust the available Infty force to support Stoneman and repair the East Tenn and Va road as far as the Watauga bridge for the present. It will be necessary for Gen Hatch to remain at Eastport for horses to mount his Div and as his force is strong enough to hold that point for the present I have not ordered any Infty there, but will await the development of events in Miss and Alabama GH Thomas 130 pm Beckwith Nashville Mch 6th 1865 1030 am 6th for Lt Gen Grant. I have an officer at Corinth Miss to receive prisoners of war but none have been delivered <deletion>do nd</deletion> to him yet. I will report the moment I hear from him GH Thomas MGen
INFO 7806 :: Page 148 :: 2.30 P. M. 6.10 P. M. City Pt. Va Mar 6. 1865. Secy of War. ---- Deserters today report that Sheridan has cut the James river Canal ---- As Richmond papers have determined not to give us news I will have to report such as is obtained through Scouts deserters & refugees to be taken for what it is worth US Grant 4 P. M. Pm. 6.20 P. M. City Pt. Va Mar 6. 1865. Secy of War. Capt. A. J. Smith 8th US Infy, now on duty at West Point has been appointed Col. of one of the new Regts of Ills. Vols. I would respy ask that leave of absence be granted to him to accept the appointment His regt I understand is at Chicago ready to take the field US Grant Lt Gen 7.30 PM 8 PM City Pt Va mar 6. 1865 Br Gen Hoffman C. G. Pris You may now discontinue sending rebel prisoners for exchange except by the regular flag of truce boat, Steamer New York US Grant Lt Gen
INFO 7807 :: Page 149 :: WR Plum City Point Mch 7th 1865 City Point 930pm 7th for Gen GH Thomas I think it will be advisable now for you to repair the RRoad in East Tenn and throw a good force up to Bulls gap and fortify there. Supplies at Knoxville could all = ways begot forward as required. With Bulls Gap fortified you can occupy as outposts about all of East Tenn and be prepared if it should be required of you in the spring to make a campaign toward Lynchburg or in to NC. I do not think Stoneman should break the road until he gets into Va unless it should be to cut off rolling stock that may be caught west of that ---- US Grant Lt Genl 1240 pm Cumberland Md Mch 7th 1865 Cumberland 11 AM for Maj Gen Halleck ---- Genl! detachment returned to Winchester from Strasburg last night nothing heard or seen of an enemy a Sergeant captured from Sheridan at New Market afterward escaped and returned to our lines last night says the people told him of Earlys defeat WS Hancocks Maj Genl
INFO 7808 :: Page 150 :: 1 pm City Point Mch 7th 1865 1230 pm 7th to Br Gen Hoffman CGP The enemy are putting all their returned prisoners into the ranks of the Eastern army without regard to the organization to which they belong. As the men returned to us are unfit for duty I want all of the same class in our hands returned before any more well men are sent back US Grant Lt Gen 4.20 P. M Cumberland Md Mar 7th 65 10 am, for Bvt Br Genl Morgan Hd Qrs 1st Corps Genl. Genl H. will not stay here at present but will return he is only waiting for you to come here to finish up the business ---- The Genl does not wish the officers ordered before the board of examination so fast as to interfere with any recruiting matters ---- Genl Carroll would be very glad if you could bring Mrs Carroll here with you sig W. G Mitchell Bvt Col & . A. D C such
INFO 8617 :: Page 139 :: B & O RR the forces at Bulltown have been notified of this fact & will be on the watch for them I have sent Genl Lightburn to Clarksburg sig S S Carroll Bvt maj Gen 11 AM 1120 AM City Pt Va Mar 3rd 1865 City Pt V Mar 11.am 3rd 1865 Secy of War I think though I am not positively advised of the fact , Sherman & Schofield are in communication and both therefore perfectly secure U. S. Grant Lt Genl 1 pm City Point Mch 3d 1865 1230 pm 3d Secy War . A great many deserters are coming in from the enemy bringing their arms with them expecting the pay for them as the means of a little ready cash . would there be any objection to amending my order so as to allow this ? Now that the sources of supply are cut off from the enemy it is a great object to deprive the enemy of present supply of arms US Grant
INFO 8618 :: Page 140 :: 720 pm City Point Mch 3d 1865 6pm 3rd for Secy War. the following communication has <insertion>just</insertion> been recd. from Genl Lee " Hd Qrs C S Armies 2d March 1865 . Gen Grant Comd'g USS Armies . Genl : Lt Genl Longstreet has informed me that in a recent conversation between himself and Major Gen Ord as to the possibility of arriving at a satisfactory adjustment of the present unhappy difficulties by means of a military convention . Genl Ord stated that if I desired to have an interview with you on the subject , you would not decline , provided I had authority to act . sincerely desiring to leave nothing untried which may put an end to the calamities of war , I propose to meet you at such convenient time and place as you may designate , with the hope that up - on an inter = change of views , it may be practicable to submit the subjects of controversy between belligerents to a convention of the kind mentioned , in such event , I am authorized to do what ever the result of the proposed interview may render necessary or advisable , should you accede to this proposition . I would suggest that , if agreeable to you , we meet at the place selected by Genls Ord & Longstreet for their interview , At 11 am on Monday next . Very respect fully your Obt Svt (signed) R E Lee " Ord met Genl Longstreet a few days since at the <insertion>request</insertion> of the latter to arrange for the exchange of citizen prisoners improperly captured he had
INFO 8619 :: Page 141 :: my authority to do so and to arrange definitely for such as were confined in his Dept arrange ments for all others to be submitted for approval . a general converse tion ensued on the subject of the war & it has induced the above letter . I have not returned any reply but promised to do so at noon tomorrow I respectfully request instructions . US Grant Lt Genl 910 pm Winchester Mch 3d 1865 Winchester 830 pm 3d Mch to Gen Halleck . Since I can not use Genl Carroll as I proposed on account of the error concerning his promotion I must either go to Cumberland and look after the Dept of West Va or send Stevenson back there which I do not care to do . unless there = fore there is some special reason for keeping me here I shall leave here for Cumberland as soon as practicable leaving Genl Emory in the immediate command of the troops here and along the military RR . Owing to the uncertainty concerning Sheridan I shall leave his HdQrs here taking with me only his Adjt Genl . Should Sheridan not return I shall then make some changes in the disposition of troops in this vicinity as suggested in dispatch of the 28th ulto I shall of course wait until it is officially settled that Sheridan will not return here WS Hancock M Genl
INFO 8620 :: Page 142 :: 1030 pm City Point Mch 3 1865 930 pm 3d To Genl George H Sharp Asst Pro Mar three ninety , 20th street Wash ---- send a good guide to Ft Monroe to ac - company the expedition to the " Northern neck " He must leave on the Baltimore boat so as to reach Ft Monroe on Sunday morning the 5th ---- US Grant Lt Genl 1120 am Balt Mch 4th 1865 11 am for Gen Halleck One of our most intelligent detectives reports that he has discovered that the rebels intended a raid from Fairfax in Washn today but that one of the rebel who has been in Washn and Balto returned to Fairfax yesterday to warn them that he thought the military authorities in Washn were prepared for them and that the raid had better be postponed . The friends of the party who has gone to Fairfax to warn the rebels fear he may not get there in time and that the raiders would attempt to reach Washn . I thought best to give you the information WW Morris Br Genl
INFO 8621 :: Page 143 :: 12 M Nashville Mch 4 1865 9 AM 4th Gen Halleck <insertion>Gen</insertion> Hobsons Div will require to be entirely remounted . The horses belonging to it having been taken to remount the divn which Genl Wilson takes with him . Gen Hatch should be remounted first . The horses which come in afterwards might be divided between Johnsons Cavalry in middle Tenn and Hobsons in Ky . GH Thomas M Gen 4.30 Pm 7 Pm City Pt. Va Mar. 4 1865 Secy of War ---- Your dispatch of 12 midnight 3rd recd ---- I have a letter to Genl Lee copy of which will be sent to you by tomorrows mail ---- I can assure you that no act of the Enemy will prevent me press = sing all advantages gained to the utmost of my ability ; neither will under any circumstances exceed my authority or in any way Embarras the Govt. ---- It was because I had no right to meet Genl Lee on the subject proposed by him that I referred the matter for instructions US Grant Lt Genl
